Libraries used by the capture helper (capture-helper/), each under a permissive licence:

- windows (Microsoft's Rust bindings for the Windows API), MIT OR Apache-2.0. https://github.com/microsoft/windows-rs
- png (PNG image encoder and decoder), MIT OR Apache-2.0. https://github.com/image-rs/image-png
- serde and serde_json (reading and writing the helper's JSON messages), MIT OR Apache-2.0. https://serde.rs

Each of these brings in smaller libraries of its own (35 Rust crates in all). One of them, unicode-ident, also
carries the Unicode licence for its data tables, which is permissive. "Check Licences.bat" reads the licence of
every one and refuses GPL and AGPL.
